# Most Common Pentesting Tools in Kali Linux

Kali Linux comes pre-loaded with hundreds of penetration testing and security tools. Here’s a list of the most popular and widely used, with short descriptions and download/reference links.

---

## 1. Wireshark
- **Use:** Network protocol analyzer (packet capture and analysis)
- **Docs:** https://www.wireshark.org/docs/
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install wireshark`

## 2. Metasploit Framework
- **Use:** Exploitation framework, vulnerability research, development, and executing exploit code
- **Docs:** https://docs.metasploit.com/
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install metasploit-framework`

## 3. Nmap
- **Use:** Network mapper/scanner for discovering hosts and services
- **Docs:** https://nmap.org/book/inst-windows.html
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install nmap`

## 4. Burp Suite Community Edition
- **Use:** Web vulnerability scanner and proxy for attacking web apps
- **Docs:** https://portswigger.net/burp/documentation
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install burpsuite`

## 5. John the Ripper
- **Use:** Password cracker
- **Docs:** https://www.openwall.com/john/doc/
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install john`

## 6. Aircrack-ng
- **Use:** Wireless network security auditing (WEP/WPA cracking)
- **Docs:** https://www.aircrack-ng.org/doku.php?id=documentation
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install aircrack-ng`

## 7. Hydra
- **Use:** Network login cracker for numerous protocols
- **Docs:** https://github.com/vanhauser-thc/thc-hydra
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install hydra`

## 8. sqlmap
- **Use:** Automated SQL injection and database takeover tool
- **Docs:** https://github.com/sqlmapproject/sqlmap/wiki
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install sqlmap`

## 9. Netcat
- **Use:** Swiss army knife for networking (debug, connect, transfer)
- **Docs:** https://nc110.sourceforge.io/
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install netcat`

## 10. Nikto
- **Use:** Web server vulnerability scanner
- **Docs:** https://cirt.net/Nikto2
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install nikto`

## 11. theHarvester
- **Use:** OSINT gathering for emails, domains, hosts
- **Docs:** https://github.com/laramies/theHarvester
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install theharvester`

## 12. Gobuster
- **Use:** Directory and file brute-forcing on web servers
- **Docs:** https://github.com/OJ/gobuster
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install gobuster`

## 13. Enum4linux
- **Use:** Windows/Samba enumeration tool
- **Docs:** https://github.com/CiscoCXSecurity/enum4linux
- **Kali Install:** `sudo apt install enum4linux`

---

### How to List All Tools in Kali
```bash
apt list --installed | grep kali
```
or browse: https://tools.kali.org/tools-listing

**Note:** Most tools can be installed with `sudo apt install <toolname>` if not already present.
